 The desktop project references the original `SnowPakTool` project and calls its `CacheBlockReader`, `CacheBlockWriter`, and `ZipPakHelper` classes. It targets .NET 10 Windows Forms.
 
-The **Game data → Trucks-Cargo** sub-tab lists cargo types and carrier variants from the active workspace, including DLC and sparse workspace updates. Use the shared double-Shift search for cargo names, types, variants, content packs and properties; click column headers to sort. The table shows the defined cargo length, sum of addon physics body masses, and cargo value. Log cargo length represents carrier slots; body mass can include carrier parts. Blank numeric values mean the value is not explicitly defined. Select a row for its localized description and all attributes from the cargo type and addon source files. **Reload cargo** refreshes the workspace data after external edits. This catalog is read-only.
+The **Game data → Trucks-Cargo** sub-tab lists cargo types and carrier variants from the active workspace, including DLC and sparse workspace updates. Use the shared double-Shift search for cargo names, types, variants, content packs and properties; click column headers to sort. The table shows the defined cargo length, loose weight (per cargo unit), packed weight (sum of addon physics body masses), and cargo value. Log cargo length represents carrier slots; body mass can include carrier parts. Blank numeric values mean the value is not explicitly defined. Select a row for its localized description and attributes from the cargo type, packed addon, matching loose models and referenced loose body templates. Loose models are matched by cargo type and slot count; static scenery is excluded. For logs, loose weight is one individual log and packed weight is the complete load. Missing or unresolved weights and differing loose-model weights remain blank. Simple loose body mass templates are resolved; full file inheritance and complex body template hierarchies remain unresolved. To increase both weights, multiply every packed body mass and the matching loose model body masses by the same factor; prefer a local Mass override over changing a shared template. **Reload cargo** refreshes the workspace data after external edits. This catalog is read-only.
 
 The **Game data → Regions-Trucks** sub-tab reads truck placements from `[scene]/data_for_ssl.bin` inside installed `level_*.pak` files, or from extracted `level_*/[scene]/data_for_ssl.bin` folders. It detects common Steam install locations; **Map folder** can be changed manually. Select one or more region tiles in the top row to populate the table below. Selected tiles are highlighted. The **Obtainable** and **Mission** checkboxes independently control those truck groups; unverified rows always remain visible for review. Double-tap **Shift** to open the same search overlay as Tier List: at least three characters highlight matches and scrolls to the first; **Enter** selects a match. **Esc**, clicking elsewhere, switching windows, or leaving the page closes the overlay. Search covers all visible table values, hover details, evidence, source paths and region tile text; Tier List also searches tier/group names and descriptions. Search does not hide rows. Each placement remains a separate row, so collectible and mission-only copies of the same model are distinguishable.
 
